&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Consumer Support team partners closely with Product, Engineering, Legal, Compliance, Regulatory, Localisation, Operations Technology, and other Operations teams to build and scale support for Link and Crypto Onramp products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the Consumer Support team, you will develop a deep understanding of Stripe’s consumer product suite and identify opportunities to resolve consumer pain points at scale. You will influence Product and Engineering roadmaps, shape support strategies, and build scalable operations for new and existing consumer products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is a highly visible, senior individual contributor (IC) role. While you will influence senior leadership and set strategic direction, you are also the primary driver of execution. You will need to zoom out to design the long-term vision, and zoom in to manage the details—building templates, tracking deliverables, writing documentation, and directly unblocking cross-functional teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead or partner with cross-functional teams, including Product, Engineering, Legal, Compliance, Support, Operations Technology, and Vendor Management, to define operational requirements for new Link, Stripe Managed Payment, and Crypto Onramp products, features, and experiments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Engineering to build the infrastructure and tooling required to launch and scale consumer operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the voice of the consumer and advocate for product improvements that address recurring pain points and their root causes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop support strategies that improve the consumer experience and increase adoption of effective self-service tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and deliver operational improvements that enable Consumer Support to scale efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to surface insights, prioritize opportunities, and measure the impact of operational and product changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver a high-quality consumer experience while meeting applicable local, consumer-protection, and regulatory requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree in business, management, economics, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in strategy and operations, consulting, program management, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in highly cross-functional roles spanning strategy, analysis, and operations in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program management skills, including experience leading complex programs from strategy through execution and delivering measurable business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and critical-thinking skills, with the ability to derive insights from data and translate them into action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain complex topics clearly to leaders and partners across Product, Engineering, and Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience aligning stakeholders with different priorities and driving commitment toward shared outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to bring structure to complex, ambiguous problems and solve them using first-principles thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to execute independently with minimal guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in SQL, including writing queries and analysing large datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI tools to improve analysis, automate workflows, or increase team efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Manager, Global Partner Programs, you’ll turn GitLab’s ecosystem strategy into repeatable programs that help partners create value across the full customer lifecycle: Acquire, Commit, and Consume. You’ll own a portfolio of global partner program workstreams, such as partner sourcing, services attach, adoption, renewals, managed service providers (MSPs), global systems integrators (GSIs), hyperscaler, and marketplace motions, and make them clear, usable, and measurable for partners and sellers across regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a strategic individual contributor role. You’ll lead through expertise and influence rather than direct reports. You’ll partner with Ecosystem Sales, Partner Operations, Finance, Legal, Marketing, Product, Customer Success, and Enablement to launch and improve programs, recommend changes to incentives and policy, and connect program activity to pipeline, revenue, and customer outcomes. In your first year, you’ll focus on building a clear roadmap for your portfolio, simplifying partner requirements and rules of engagement, and setting up consistent reporting on program performance. As the team grows, this role may expand to include leading partner program managers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the roadmap, priorities, and execution for an assigned set of global partner programs across Acquire, Commit, and Consume, within agreed strategy, policy, and budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate requirements, milestones, owners, and risks across Ecosystem Sales, Partner Operations, Finance, Legal, Marketing, Services, Customer Success, Product, Enablement, and regional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the partner journey from onboarding and capability building through activation, co-selling, adoption, and expansion, turning partner and field feedback into prioritized program improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the design and rollout of partner incentives, including margin, rebates, market development funds (MDF), deal registration, services attach, and consumption, and build business cases with Finance and Ecosystem leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain program guides, eligibility rules, approval flows, and documentation, partnering with Legal and Finance so programs are compliant, auditable, and easy to understand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create playbooks, launch materials, and training with Enablement and regional teams to drive adoption of new programs and commercial changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success measures for each program, such as partner-sourced pipeline, services attach, adoption, and incentive use, and partner with Revenue Operations to report on them consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use performance data to recommend investment changes, reduce exceptions and manual work, and escalate decisions that go beyond your scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in partner programs, channel strategy, alliances, ecosystem operations, or a related go-to-market function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of taking complex programs from design through launch, adoption, measurement, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of partner economics, including incentives, deal registration, MDF, services programs, co-selling, and rules of engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead global, cross-functional work without direct authority, setting clear owners, decisions, and escalation paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical judgment and the ability to connect program activity to pipeline, revenue, and customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication, including the ability to make complex commercial concepts simple for partners and sellers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program management discipline across prioritization, dependencies, risk, and follow-through, with a bias toward practical execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SaaS, cloud, DevOps, or AI partner ecosystems; consumption-based pricing; or hyperscaler marketplace and co-sell programs is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to candidates with transferable experience who can build trust across teams and turn strategy into results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Ecosystem team helps GitLab grow through partners, including GSIs, MSPs, professional services partners, resellers, and cloud hyperscalers. We’re building a more intentional partner model that goes beyond the transaction to create value across sourcing, co-selling, deployment, adoption, services, and consumption. We work asynchronously across regions as part of a remote-first company, with occasional travel for partner meetings, planning, and program launches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Zipline&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is the world’s largest and most experienced drone delivery service. We are on a mission to serve all humans equally by ensuring access to food, medicine and essential goods anytime, anywhere. We design, build, and operate the world’s largest autonomous logistics system, delivering critical supplies quickly and reliably. Today, Zipline operates on four continents, makes a delivery somewhere in the world every 30 seconds, and has completed millions of deliveries to date, including blood, vaccines, medical supplies, food, and retail products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include the world’s largest and most prominent healthcare systems, governments, retailers, restaurants and global businesses who rely on us to save lives, reduce emissions, increase economic opportunity, and provide delivery from point A to point B as fast as possible. The drone is only 15% of what we’ve built to enable seamless, reliable, global operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our system strengthens supply chains, reduces congestion, and gives people time back. With more than 140 million commercial autonomous miles safely flown, Zipline is redefining access to healthcare, consumer products, and food across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at a global scale and are looking for practical problem solvers who thrive on real-world challenges and rapid growth. Our team is motivated by building systems that have a direct, meaningful impact on people’s lives and by scaling the future of logistics. We are seeking people who sculpt from first principles, enjoy facing adversity, and can do the impossible at record breaking speeds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You and The Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;17&quot;&gt;Zipline is looking for a Technical Program Manager, Facilities to deliver the spaces and infrastructure that support our engineering, test, manufacturing, and workplace teams. You will lead facilities projects from initial requirements and feasibility through design, permitting, construction, commissioning, and operational handoff, with accountability for scope, budget, schedule, and readiness for use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;424&quot;&gt;Working closely with Facilities, engineering stakeholders, &lt;span class=&quot;acronym-highlight&quot;&gt;EHS&lt;/span&gt;, IT, and external partners, you will translate evolving business needs into executable project plans. Your work will include new facilities, renovations, equipment installations, utility upgrades, and relocations, coordinating the building systems and operational dependencies required to bring each space into service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;808&quot;&gt;We are looking for someone who combines technical judgment with hands-on program execution. You ask why a requirement exists, challenge assumptions with evidence, and find practical ways to meet competing needs. You can create clarity from incomplete information, hold partners accountable, and deliver projects in active environments where safety and operational continuity matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Lead a portfolio of facilities capital projects, establishing scope, success criteria, budgets, schedules, and accountable owners from project initiation through handoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Partner with internal teams to define space, equipment, utility, and operational requirements. Separate essential needs from preferences and turn them into clear project scopes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Coordinate architects, engineers, contractors, and specialty vendors through design, permitting, procurement, and construction. Set deliverables and resolve gaps between disciplines and project packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Use technical judgment to evaluate building-system capacity, equipment requirements, constructability, and maintainability. Challenge unnecessary scope and develop alternatives that improve cost or schedule while meeting safety and performance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Build integrated project schedules that account for permits, long-lead equipment, utility connections, shutdowns, and occupancy requirements. Identify critical dependencies and drive timely decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Develop requests for proposals and evaluate bids with Procurement and project partners. Track commitments, forecasts, and change orders, and make clear recommendations on scope and spending decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Coordinate site work, equipment installations, relocations, and shutdowns with Facilities, EHS, IT, and operating teams to protect safety and minimize disruption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Maintain clear reporting on milestones, budgets, risks, and decisions. Escalate issues with a recommended path forward and drive recovery plans when delivery is at risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Lead readiness reviews and coordinate commissioning, inspections, punch-list completion, and handoff. Ensure Facilities and end users receive the documentation, training, and maintenance information needed to operate the space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3086&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;A track record of managing complex facilities, infrastructure, or construction programs from initial scope through operational handoff, with accountability for budget, schedule, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3086&quot;&gt;A technical foundation in mechanical, electrical, structural, architectural, or facilities engineering, construction management, or a related discipline, gained through education or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3086&quot;&gt;Experience coordinating multidisciplinary consultants, contractors, vendors, and internal stakeholders, including work in active manufacturing, laboratory, R&amp;amp;D, or other technical environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3086&quot;&gt;The ability to read technical drawings, assess building-system and equipment dependencies, and ask the questions needed to identify design or execution risks. Working knowledge of permitting, construction sequencing, and commissioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3086&quot;&gt;Strong program management skills, including scope development, estimating, scheduling, bid evaluation, change management, and risk resolution across multiple concurrent projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3086&quot;&gt;Clear communication and sound judgment when priorities compete. The ability to explain technical trade-offs, recommend a path forward, and influence teams without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3086&quot;&gt;A hands-on approach to execution, curiosity about how facilities support the business, and ownership of problems through resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Else You Need To Know&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting cash range for this role is $160,000.00 - $205,000.00. Please note that this is a target, starting cash range for a candidate who meets the minimum qualifications for this role. The final cash pay for this role will depend on a variety of factors, including a specific candidate&#39;s experience, qualifications, skills, working location, and projected impact. The total compensation package for this role may also include: equity compensation; overtime pay; discretionary annual or performance bonuses; sales incentives; benefits such as medical, dental and vision insurance; paid time off; and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws or our own sensibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value diversity at Zipline and welcome applications from those who are traditionally underrepresented in tech. If you like the sound of this position but are not sure if you are the perfect fit, please apply!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Voluntary Self-Identification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;For government reporting purposes, we ask candidates to respond to the below self-identification survey. Completion of the form is entirely voluntary. Whatever your decision, it will not be considered in the hiring process or thereafter. Any information that you do provide will be recorded and maintained in a confidential file.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;As set forth in Zipline ’s Equal Employment Opportunity policy, we do not discriminate on the basis of any protected group status under any applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
